---
import LegalPage from '../layouts/LegalPage.astro';

/**
 * /privacy
 *
 * Written to be read, not to be survived. The site is a static build with no
 * accounts, no basket and no ad tech, so most of a standard privacy policy does
 * not apply, and saying that plainly is worth more than a page of boilerplate
 * that describes a company we are not.
 *
 * Anything asserted here has to stay true of the actual build. If analytics,
 * a newsletter or an embedded booking widget ever ships, this page and
 * /cookies change in the same commit.
 */
const SECTIONS = [
  { id: 'who-we-are', label: 'Who we are' },
  { id: 'what-we-collect', label: 'What we collect' },
  { id: 'what-we-do-not-collect', label: 'What we do not collect' },
  { id: 'why-we-use-it', label: 'Why we use it' },
  { id: 'legal-bases', label: 'Legal bases' },
  { id: 'who-sees-it', label: 'Who sees it' },
  { id: 'where-it-is-held', label: 'Where it is held' },
  { id: 'how-long-we-keep-it', label: 'How long we keep it' },
  { id: 'your-rights', label: 'Your rights' },
  { id: 'children', label: 'Children' },
  { id: 'other-sites', label: 'Other sites' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'Changes' },
  { id: 'contact', label: 'Contact' },
];
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy"
  seoTitle="Privacy · Visit Moganshan"
  description="What Visit Moganshan collects, why, who sees it and how to ask us to delete it. A static travel guide with no advertising trackers and no accounts."
  standfirst="Visit Moganshan is a travel guide, not a booking platform. We collect very little, we sell none of it, and this page says exactly what happens to what we do hold."
  updated="2026-08-05"
  sections={SECTIONS}
>
  <h2 id="who-we-are">Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Visit Moganshan is published by BeyondBorder Group Ltd, a company registered in Hong Kong.
    BeyondBorder Group Ltd is the data controller for this site and for messages sent to us through
    it. How the site is funded, and whether we hold any commercial interest in a property we write
    about, is set out on the <a href="/about">About page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="what-we-collect">What we collect</h2>
  <p>There are two ways your information reaches us, and only two.</p>
  <p>
    <strong>What you send us.</strong> If you write to us, pitch a property, correct a page or make a
    trade or media enquiry, we receive whatever you put in that message: your name, your email
    address, the company you work for if you mention it, and the content of the message itself.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What your browser sends our host.</strong> Serving a page leaves a server log entry. That
    entry can include your IP address, the page requested, the time of the request, the referring
    page, and your browser and device type. These logs are produced by our hosting provider as part
    of delivering and protecting the site. We use them to keep the site up, to size images and pages
    for the devices that actually load them, and to investigate abuse.
  </p>

  <h2 id="what-we-do-not-collect">What we do not collect</h2>
  <p>
    We do not run advertising trackers, remarketing pixels or social media tracking scripts. We do
    not buy contact lists. We do not build profiles of readers, we do not sell or rent anything about
    you, and we do not ask for special category information such as health, religion or political
    views. The site sets no cookies of its own and asks you to dismiss no banner, which is explained
    in full in the <a href="/cookies">cookie policy</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    We take no payments on this site. There is no checkout here, so we never see a card number, and
    any booking you make happens on a hotel or operator system under that company's own policy.
  </p>

  <h2 id="why-we-use-it">Why we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To answer you. A message you send is used to reply and to follow up on that conversation.</li>
    <li>
      To keep the guide accurate. A correction you send may change a page. We do not publish your
      name or contact details when we act on one unless you have asked us to credit you.
    </li>
    <li>
      To run and defend the site. Server logs support uptime, performance work, and blocking abuse
      such as scraping and attempted attacks.
    </li>
    <li>
      To meet obligations. Correspondence connected to a commercial or contractual matter is kept as
      long as accounting and legal duties require.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not use what you send us for automated decision making, and we do not add correspondents to
    a mailing list on the strength of a single enquiry.
  </p>

  <h2 id="legal-bases">Legal bases</h2>
  <p>
    We process personal data under Hong Kong's Personal Data (Privacy) Ordinance. Where a reader is
    in the United Kingdom or the European Economic Area, we also apply the standards of the UK GDPR
    and the EU GDPR, and we rely on these bases:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Legitimate interests</strong> for replying to enquiries, keeping the guide accurate,
      and operating and securing the site. Our interest in running a working, factual travel guide is
      balanced against the very small amount of information involved.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Contract</strong> where we are dealing with a trade, media or commercial arrangement
      and need your details to carry it out.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Consent</strong> where you have specifically asked to receive something from us. You
      can withdraw it at any time and we act on that immediately.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Legal obligation</strong> where the law requires us to keep or produce records.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="who-sees-it">Who sees it</h2>
  <p>
    Inside our company, only the people who need your message in order to act on it. Outside it, only
    service providers who make the site work, each bound by contract and confidentiality: our hosting
    and content delivery provider, our email provider, and, where a matter requires it, professional
    advisers such as lawyers and accountants.
  </p>
  <p>
    We will disclose information where the law compels us to, and to protect the rights or safety of
    readers, our staff or the public. Beyond that, nobody sees it. We do not share reader
    correspondence with hotels or operators, including when your message is about them, unless you
    ask us to put you in touch.
  </p>

  <h2 id="where-it-is-held">Where it is held</h2>
  <p>
    The site is hosted on servers operated by our provider and delivered worldwide from an edge
    network, so a page you load may be served from a location near you. Email and correspondence are
    held on providers whose infrastructure sits in Hong Kong, the European Economic Area and the
    United States.
  </p>
  <p>
    That means information may be transferred outside your own country. Where personal data of
    readers in the United Kingdom or the European Economic Area is transferred, we rely on the
    providers' standard contractual clauses and equivalent safeguards, and we keep the volume of data
    involved as small as the service allows.
  </p>

  <h2 id="how-long-we-keep-it">How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>General correspondence: up to two years from our last exchange, then deleted.</li>
    <li>
      Commercial, trade and media correspondence: for the life of the arrangement plus seven years,
      which is what accounting and tax rules require of us.
    </li>
    <li>
      Server logs: retained by our hosting provider for a short operational window, typically no more
      than 30 days, unless an entry is needed for a live security investigation.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    When a retention period ends, the record is deleted. We do not keep anything on the theory that
    it may prove useful one day.
  </p>

  <h2 id="your-rights">Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask us to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>confirm whether we hold personal data about you, and give you a copy of it;</li>
    <li>correct anything inaccurate;</li>
    <li>delete what we hold, where no legal duty requires us to keep it;</li>
    <li>restrict or object to how we use it;</li>
    <li>provide it in a portable form; and</li>
    <li>withdraw consent you previously gave, without affecting what we did before you withdrew it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Write to <a href="mailto:privacy@visitmoganshan.com">privacy@visitmoganshan.com</a>. We answer
    within 30 days, and there is no charge. We may ask you to confirm your identity before we release
    a copy of anything, because handing your data to somebody who claims to be you would be the worse
    failure.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are unhappy with our answer, you can complain to the Office of the Privacy Commissioner
    for Personal Data in Hong Kong, to the Information Commissioner's Office in the United Kingdom,
    or to your own national supervisory authority in the European Economic Area. We would rather you
    told us first, but it is your right either way.
  </p>

  <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
  <p>
    This site is written for adults planning travel. We do not knowingly collect personal data from
    children under 13. If you believe a child has sent us personal information, write to us and we
    will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="other-sites">Other sites</h2>
  <p>
    We link out to hotels, operators, rail and airline booking systems, official tourism bodies and
    map services. Once you follow a link, you are on somebody else's site under their privacy policy
    and their cookie practices, over which we have no control and for which we take no
    responsibility. It is worth reading theirs before you book.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
  <p>
    When this policy changes, the date at the top of the page changes with it, and the change ships
    in the same release as whatever prompted it. If a change materially affects how we treat
    information you have already sent us, we will say so on this page rather than leave you to spot
    the difference.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Privacy questions and rights requests go to
    <a href="mailto:privacy@visitmoganshan.com">privacy@visitmoganshan.com</a>. Anything else about
    the guide goes through the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. Our terms are on the
    <a href="/terms">terms page</a>, and what we do about cookies is on the
    <a href="/cookies">cookie page</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
